-- title:
--   Regular Moment Witness with Bounded Cutoff Testing
-- statement:
--   This formalizes the regular moment construction together with bounded weak cutoff testing associated with Lemma A.5 of Letwin (arXiv:2607.24164v1).
--
--   Under the same assumptions as the regular moment witness—$n>0$, $\kappa>0$, compact convex $K$ with nonempty interior, smooth $W$, convexity of $W-\frac\kappa2\|\cdot\|^2$, the density representation of an isotropic probability measure $\mu$, and the stated measure identity—there exist $u,L,LF,T$ carrying the full regular moment, weak Hessian evolution, bounded weak Hessian testing, and weak cutoff payloads.
--
--   In particular, there are $c,C$ and cutoffs $\chi_R$ with all properties listed for `exists_regular_moment_weak_cutoffs_readable`, including $0\le\chi_R\le1$, compact support, pointwise monotonicity and convergence to $1$, tilted-measure integrability of the generator, and the bound $\int|L\chi_R|\,d(e^{-u}dx)\le C/R$.
--
--   Furthermore, for every $r\ge1$, every locally integrable globally bounded weak function $\eta$, every family of compact-locally $L^2$ weak coordinate derivatives $a_i$, and every bound $C_\eta$, the products are integrable and the rough cutoff identity holds:
--
--   $$
--   \int \eta(x)L\chi_r(x)e^{-u(x)}\,dx
--   =-\int\sum_{i,j}(\nabla^2u(x))^{-1}_{ij}a_i(x)\partial_j\chi_r(x)e^{-u(x)}\,dx.
--   $$
--
--   This is an existential package retaining the common witness and cutoff family while adding the universal bounded weak-test identity.
